 ## Background
-Dynamic Field Blending was introduced in the TöRF (Time-of-Flight Radiance Fields) paper by [S1, unofficial]. It is part of the DyNeRF family of methods for dynamic scene view synthesis. The method builds on the idea of decomposing the scene into static and dynamic components and blending their contributions [S1, unofficial].
